hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5128","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Umra becomes the property of the one to whom a man has given it as Umra. Ruqba becomes the property of the one to whom it has been given as Ruqba."
"5129","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""ʿUmrá is permissible."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2626)"
"5130","""Yahya bin Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: 'Abu Salamah bin 'Abdur-Rahman narrated to me, he said: ""I heard Jabir say: 'The Messenger of Allah said: ""A lifelong gift belongs to the one to whom it was given.""'""'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3750)"
"5131","""There is no lifelong gift. Whoever is given something as a lifelong gift, it belongs to him."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3752)"
"5132","The method of 'Umariyyah will be according to the method of inheritance (that is, the rulings of inheritance will apply to it)."
"5133","It was narrated from Zaid bin Thabit that the Prophet ruled that 'Umra (a gift given for life) belongs to the heir. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3722)"
"5134","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The person who is given land as 'Umra, it will go to his heirs."
"5135","The Prophet ﷺ said: If anyone is given life-tenancy, it belongs to him and to his descendants. His descendants who inherit him will inherit from it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3551)"
"5136","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to the Ansar: Do not give your wealth as 'Umra (life grant), because whatever is given to someone as 'Umra during his lifetime becomes his property, and after his death, it will go to his heirs."
"5137","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: If anyone has property given him in life-tenancy for the use of himself and his descendants, it belongs to the one to whom it is given and does not return to the one who gave it, because he gave a gift which may be inherited. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3553)"
"5138","“I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever gives a lifelong grant to a man, it belongs to him (the recipient) and to his heirs. His (the giver's) words put an end to his right to it, and it belongs to the one to whom it was given for life and to his heirs.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2380)"
"5139","The life-tenancy which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ allowed was only that one should say: It is for you and your descendants. When he says: It is yours as long as you live, it returns to its owner. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3555)"
"5140","""Abu Az-Zubair informed me that he heard Jabir saying: 'The Messenger of Allah said: ""Whoever is given something on the basis of 'Umra it belongs to him for the rest of his life and after he dies.""'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 3735)"
"5141","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade making vows and giving anything as 'Umra or Ruqba, and there is a specific reason for this: the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) wanted the wealth of Muslims to remain with them. This does not mean that acting upon these three things is not permissible when it is done in obedience and not in disobedience. The reason is that the noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) had settled in Madinah Munawwarah, where they did not own any land, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) disliked that they give anything as Ruqba or 'Umra. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) wanted their wealth to remain with them because they needed it. This does not mean that acting upon these two things is not permissible at all."
"5142","""Zakariyya was a carpenter."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2150)"
"5143","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Pick the black ones, for they are purer. We asked: Did you tend sheep? The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Every prophet has tended sheep."
"5144","I used to eat them in the days when I used to herd goats. The people asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! Did you also herd goats? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: Every prophet who was sent has herded goats."
"5145","The morning after the marriage, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) invited people. Those people ate food and then left. Some of them remained seated with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). They sat for quite a while, then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up and left, and I went along with him. The purpose was that those people would also get up and leave. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) kept walking, and I went with him. When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) reached the threshold of Sayyidah Aisha's (may Allah be pleased with her) room, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) thought that those people must have left. He returned, and I also returned with him. When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) reached the house of Sayyidah Zaynab (may Allah be pleased with her), those people were still sitting there. They had not gotten up and left, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) returned again, and I also returned with him. Then, when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) reached the door of Sayyidah Aisha's (may Allah be pleased with her) room, he thought that those people must have left. He returned, and I also returned, and those people had left. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had a curtain placed between those people and himself, and at that time the verse regarding the command of hijab was revealed."
"5146","I recited Surah Al-Fatihah over him, and he was cured. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The thing most deserving for which you take compensation is the Book of Allah."
"5147","""Makhrafah Al' Abdi and I brought linens from Hajar[1] The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to us to bargain with us with some trousers. There was someone with me who weighed (the goods) in exchange for a wage. So the Prophet ﷺ said to the one weighing: 'Weigh and add more.'"" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2220)"
"5148","The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""He should not take compensation from him""—here, the prohibition is in wording, but the intent is to express recommendation and guidance, because people used to face hardship in their affairs, so giving land as a gift was considered better than renting it out. Otherwise, all Muslims are agreed upon this: it is permissible to take rent for land, except for the type which the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has prohibited."
"5149","“O Messenger of Allah, will you stay in your house in Makkah?” He said: “Has ‘Aqeel left us any houses?” 'Aqeel had inherited Abu Talib along with Talib. Neither Ja'far nor 'Ali inherited anything because they had been Muslims, and 'Aqeel and Talib had been disbelievers. So on account of that, Omar would say the believer does not inherit from the disbeliever. And Usamah said: the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said ""The Muslim does not inherit from the disbeliever nor the disbeliever from the Muslim."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2730)"
"5150","the Prophet ﷺ was treated with cupping and gave the cupper his wages. (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2164)"
"5151","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had cupping done and he paid the cupper his fee."
"5152","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The earnings of the cupper are impure, the price of a dog is impure, and the earn"
"5153","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The earnings of the cupper are impure, the earnings of a prostitute are impure,"
"5154","The Prophet (peace be upon him) refused to grant permission regarding the earnings from cupping because there was a hidden condition in it: the person performing cupping had stipulated that he would extract a specific amount of blood, but since he did not have the ability to fulfill this condition, the Prophet (peace be upon him) disliked granting permission regarding its earnings. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \""Feed it to your slave or feed it as fodder to your camel.\"" So, if the earnings f"
"5155","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade giving a camel for mating (on rent)."
"5156","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade giving a camel for mating in exchange for compensation."
"5157","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, and the earnings of a soothsayer."
"5158","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade earnings from slave girls."
"5159","That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade earnings of slave-girls. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3425)"
"5160","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: It is because of those seven dinars that came to us last evening and we have not been able to distribute them."
"5161","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever seizes even a handspan of land unjustly, on the Day of Resurrection a collar equal to seven earths will be placed around his neck."
"5162","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever seizes a span of land unjustly will have a collar of seven earths placed around his neck."
"5163",": : "" "" . Whoever usurps a span or more of land, even if he acquires that land through a false oath"
"5164","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Whoever seizes a span of land unjustly, Allah will make him dig it until he reaches the seven earths, then on the Day of Resurrection a collar will be placed around his neck which will remain until judgment is passed among the people."
"5165","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was walking between two Jamrat at that time. He said: ""Whoever acquires even a handspan of a Muslim's wealth through a false oath should be prepared to reach his abode in Hell."" In narrating this tradition, the narrator named Umar bin Abdulwahab is unique."
"5166","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Help your brother, whether he is an oppressor or he is an oppressed one."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 2443)"
"5167","""Help your brother whether he is an oppressor or oppressed."" It was said: ""O Messenger of Allah! I help him when he is oppressed. But how can I help him when he oppresses?"" He said: ""Prevent him from oppression, that is your help for him."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2255)"
"5168","The people asked: ""O Messenger of Allah! We will help the oppressed, but how should we help the oppressor?"" The Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""By preventing him from oppression."
"5169","I heard the announcer of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding looting."
"5170","“Whoever plunders is not one of us.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3937)"
"5171","I should not find anyone who has milked the milk of another's animal without that person's permission."
"5172","When one commits fornication, one is not a believer ; when one steals, one is not a believer ; when one drinks, one is not a believer ; and repentance is placed before him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4689)"
"5173","When one commits fornication, one is not a believer ; when one steals, one is not a believer ; when one drinks, one is not a believer ; and repentance is placed before him. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4689)"
"5174","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent until we realized that revelation was being sent down upon him. When revelation would come to him, he would become drowsy and sweat would appear on him. When this state ended, he asked: Where is the questioner? He replied: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I am here. I only intended good by it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good only brings good, but what the spring grows kills many animals and causes suffering to many animals. The case of the animal that eats greenery is different, for it eats until its belly is full, then it goes into the sun, where it defecates and urinates, then returns, eats again, stands up, and moves on. Whoever acquires wealth along with the right (truth), there is blessing in it for him and that wealth benefits him. Whoever acquires wealth unjustly, there is no blessing in it for him, and his example is like that person who, despite eating, does not become satisfied."
"5175","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Indeed, Allah Almighty gives respite to the oppressor until, when He seizes him, He does not let him go."" Then he recited this verse: ""Such is the seizure of your Lord when He seizes the towns while they are doing wrong. Indeed, His seizure is painful and severe."
"5176","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Beware of oppression, for on the Day of Resurrection, oppression will be in the form of darknesses. And avoid obscene speech, for Allah Almighty does not like a person who is obscene and foul-mouthed. And beware of miserliness, for miserliness destroyed those before you. It incited them to sever the ties of kinship, so they severed them. It incited them to commit si"
"5177","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Avoid obscene speech, for Allah Almighty does not like the one who is obscene and foul-mouthed. And avoid oppression, for oppression will appear as darknesses on the Day of Resurrection. And avoid miserliness, for miserliness invited those before you, so they shed each other's blood and violated the rights of kinship because of it.\"""""
"5178","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is pre-emption in every land and garden. It is not permissible to sell it until a person offers it to his partner regarding this. If he wishes, he may take it, and if he wishes, he may leave it."
"5179","He who has a partner in a dwelling or a garden, it is not lawful for him to sell that until he is permitted by his partner. If he (the partner) agrees, he should go in for that, and if he disapproves of that, he should abandon (the idea of selling it). (Using translation from Muslim 1608a)"
"5180","“The neighbor has more right to property that is near.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2495)"
"5181","The neighbor has more right to his neighbor’s property,’ I would not have sold those houses to you, because I was getting five hundred dinars for them.”"
"5182","The Prophet ﷺ said: A neighbour has the best claim to the house or land of the neighbour. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3517)"
"5183","While I was standing with Saʿd bin Abi Waqqas, Al-Miswar bin Makhrama came and put his hand on my shoulder. Meanwhile Abu Rafiʿ, the freed slave of the Prophet ﷺ came and asked Saʿd to buy from him the (two) dwellings which were in his house. Saʿd said, ""By Allah I will not buy them."" Al- Miswar said, ""By Allah, you shall buy them."" Saʿd replied, ""By Allah, I will not pay more than four thousand (Dirhams) by installments."" Abu Rafiʿ said, ""I have been offered five hundred Dinars (for it) and had I not heard the Prophet ﷺ saying, 'The neighbor has more right than anyone else because of his nearness, I would not give them to you for four-thousand (Dirhams) while I am offered five-hundred Dinars (one Dinar equals ten Dirhams) for them."" So, he sold it to Saʿd. (Using translation from Bukhārī 2258)"
"5184","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed the right to buy the neighboring property applicable to everything which is not divided, but when boundaries are fixed and separate roads made, there is no option. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3514)"
"5185","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ decreed the right to buy the neighboring property applicable to everything which is not divided, but when boundaries are fixed and separate roads made, there is no option. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3514)"
"5186","Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided the validity of preemption in every joint undivided property, but if the boundaries were well marked or the ways and streets were fixed, then there was no pre-emption. (Using translation from Bukhārī 2214)"
"5187","Messenger of Allah ﷺ decided the validity of preemption in every joint undivided property, but if the boundaries were well marked or the ways and streets were fixed, then there was no pre-emption. (Using translation from Bukhārī 2214)"
"5188","By Allah, I am certain that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that. (Using translation from Aḥmad 101)"
"5189","“I heard Jabir bin 'Abdullah say: Some men among us had extra land which they would rent out for one third or one quarter (of the crop). The Prophet ﷺ said: “Whoever has extra land, let him cultivate it (himself) or let him give it to his brother (for free, to cultivate it), and if he does not want to do that, let him keep his land.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2451)"
"5190","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever has land should cultivate it, and if he cannot do so, then he should give it to his brother (for temporary use without compensation)."
"5191","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us from doing something that was convenient for us.” I said: “What the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said is true.” He said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “What do you with your farms?” We said: “We rent them out for one third or one quarter of their yield, and a certain amount of wheat and barley.” He said: “Do not do that; cultivate them or let others cultivate them.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 2459)"
"5192","I asked Ata: Did you hear this directly from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them), that he mentioned this hadith from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He replied: Yes. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abu Walid is Saeed bin Mina Makki."
"5193","Nafiʿ reported to me that he heard Ibn ʿUmar (Allah be pleased with them) saying: We usedto give land on rent; we then abandoned this practice when we heard the hadith of Rafiʿ b. Khadij. (Using translation from Muslim 1536w)"
"5194","narrate from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade leasing out fields. Rafi' replied: Yes. After that, whenever Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) was asked about this matter, he would say: Rafi' bin Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to us that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade leasing out fields."
"5195","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not prohibit share-cropping. But he ordered that they be helpful with each other."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 1385)"
"5196","narrates: Previously, we used to lease out land, and the owner of the land would exclude a specific part of the field and the area around the water source. Sometimes, the produce of one part would be ruined while the other part would remain fine, so the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade this. Sayyiduna Rafi’ (may Allah be pleased with him) says: However, if the land is leased in exchange for a specified thing, then there is no harm in it."
"5197","narrates: Previously, land used to be leased out in exchange for produce, and sometimes for a specified portion of grain that was set aside. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade people from leasing out land in this manner. Sayyiduna Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) says: As for leasing land in exchange for gold or silver, there is no harm in that."
"5198","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) has forbidden muzabanah."
"5199","I saw Huyayy wandering around one of the ruins here.” People went and searched there, and they found the bag in that ruin. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) then ordered the execution of both sons of Abu Huqayq, one of whom was also the husband of Huyayy bin Akhtab’s daughter, Lady Safiyyah. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took their women and children as captives and distributed their wealth among the people. When he intended to exile them from there, they said: “O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), let us stay on our land. We will work here and take care of it.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and his companions did not have people who could look after the land and supervise it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave the land of Khaybar to them on the condition that they would receive half of the produce of the land, dates, and other things (and half would be given to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)), for as long as the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) wished (i.e., whenever the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) wished, he could end this agreement). Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahah (may Allah be pleased with him) used to come there every year and estimate their produce, then require them to pay half. The narrator says: They complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about the strictness of Abdullah bin Rawahah’s estimation. They had even tried to bribe him before, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “O enemies of Allah! Do you want to feed me what is unlawful? By Allah, I have come to you from the one who is dearest to me, and you are the most hated to me—even more than monkeys and pigs—but even so, my hatred for you and my love for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not make me unjust to you.” So they said: “It is because of this (honesty) that the heavens and the earth stand firm.” The narrator states: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw a green mark on both eyes of Lady Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) and asked: “O Safiyyah! Is there a reason for this green mark?” She replied: “My head was in the lap of Abu Huqayq’s son (i.e., my former husband) and I was asleep. In my dream, I saw that the moon had fallen into my lap. (Upon waking) I told my husband about it, so he slapped me and said: ‘You desire the king of Yathrib (i.e., the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)).’” Lady Safiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: “At first, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was the most disliked person to me because he had caused the killing of my husband, my father, and my brother. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) kept explaining to me, saying: ‘Your father turned all the Arabs against me. He did this, he did that (so I was compelled to fight him).’ Until the dislike I had in my heart for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was removed.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to give each of his wives eighty (80) wasqs of dates and twenty (20) wasqs of barley every year. When the caliphate of Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came, and (the Jews of Khaybar) began to deceive the Muslims and threw the son of Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) from the roof of a house, Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: “Whoever has a specific share in Khaybar, let him come so that we may distribute it among them.” Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) distributed it among those who were present at the Treaty of Hudaybiyyah and participated in the Battle of Khaybar. Their leader said: “Do not expel us (from Khaybar); let us stay here as the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) let us stay.” Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to their leader: “Do you think that I have acted contrary to the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) regarding this? What will be your condition when your mount is carrying you towards Syria?” Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) distributed the land among those who were present at the Treaty of Hudaybiyyah and participated in the Battle of Khaybar."
"5200","I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: If any of you does not leave mukhabarah, he should take notice of war from Allah and His Apostle ﷺ. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3406)"
"5201","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade us from this. He permitted us to lease out land in exchange for gold or silver."
"5202","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Whoever cultivates barren land will receive its reward, and whatever is eaten from it will be charity for that person."
"5203","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever revives barren land, he will have its reward, and whatever living being eats from it, he will have its reward."
"5204","narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever revives barren land, he will receive its reward, and whatever eats from it will be counted as charity for that person."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In this narration, there is clear evidence that when a dhimmi person revives barren land, it will not become his property, because charity is only for Muslims."
"5205","The word ""afiyah"" is used for seekers of sustenance (which is used in this hadith); this has been stated by Imam Abu Hatim."
"5206","“A house in which there are no dates, its people will go hungry.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3327)"
"5207","I heard the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, say: ""This is a cause for increase in blessing."
"5208","I about to pray that I should perform ablution?"
"5209","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""When food is served and the prayer is established, then eat the food first.\"""""
"5211","I always ate in this manner. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abu Wajzah is Yazid bin Ubaid Sa'di."
"5212","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) invited him to food and said: O my son, come forward and eat from what is in front of you, eat with your right hand, and mention the name of Allah over it."
"5213","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud, may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever forgets to mention Allah at the beginning of his meal, then whenever he remembers, he should say: 'In the name of Allah, at its beginning and at its end.' It will be as if he has started his meal anew, and whatever harm had reached him before will be prevented."
"5214","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was eating food with six of his Companions when a Bedouin came and ate it all in two bites. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘If he had said Bismillah, it would have sufficed you (all). When any one of you eats food, let him say Bismillah, and if he forgets to say Bismillah at the beginning, let him say Bismillah fi awwalihi wa akhirih (In the Name of Allah at the beginning and at the end).’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3264)"
"5215","The Prophet ﷺ said: Come near, my son, mention Allah's name, eat with your right hand and eat from what is next to you. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3777)"
"5216","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I too have come out only for this reason. Get up, both of you. Then both of them went with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) to the house of Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him). Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) used to keep food and milk, etc., saved for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). That day, he was delayed and had not come at that time. He had fed his family and gone to his date orchard to work there. When these noble ones reached the house of Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him), his wife came out. She said: Welcome to the Prophet of Allah and his companions. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked the woman: Where is Abu Ayyub? Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) heard your voice while he was working in his orchard. He came quickly and said: Welcome to the Prophet of Allah and his companions. O Prophet of Allah, you do not usually come at this time. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: You have spoken the truth. The narrator says: Then Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) went and brought every kind of date from his orchard—dry, fresh, and moist dates. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I did not want you to bring all these; you should have brought only dry dates for us. He replied: O Prophet of Allah, I wanted you to eat every kind of date, both dry and fresh. Along with this, I will also slaughter an animal for you. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If you are going to slaughter, then do not slaughter a milk-giving animal. Then he slaughtered a kid of a goat or sheep and said to his wife: You bake bread and knead the dough for us, for you make good bread. Then he took the kid and cooked it, and roasted half of it. When the food was ready, it was placed before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and his companions. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took some meat, placed it with bread, and said: O Abu Ayyub! Take this to Fatimah, for she too has not eaten for several days. Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) went to deliver that food to Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her). When these noble ones had eaten and were satisfied, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Bread and meat, dry, fresh, and moist dates—then tears flowed from his eyes. He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, these are the blessings about which you will be questioned. The command of Allah, the Exalted, is: ""On that Day, you will surely be questioned about the blessings."" () (The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said:) So these are the blessings about which you will be held accountable on the Day of Resurrection. This was burdensome for his companions, so he said: When you are granted such blessings, then stretch forth your hands and say Bismillah, and when you are satisfied, recite this: ""All praise is due to Allah alone, Who has satisfied us and bestowed blessings and favor upon us."" This will suffice for them. When they were about to leave, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him): Come to us tomorrow. Whenever any good was done to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he liked to return it. The narrator says: Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) did not hear this, so Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has instructed you to present yourself to him tomorrow. The next day, Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) gave him his slave-girl. He said: O Abu Ayyub, accept the advice of goodness regarding her, for as long as she was with us, we saw only good in her. When Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) took the slave-girl from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: Regarding the goodness the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) advised about her, I find nothing better than to set her free. So Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) set her free."
"5217","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) recite this supplication after finishing food: “All praise is due to Allah alone, abundant, pure, and blessed praise, such as cannot be dispensed with, nor left, nor can anyone do without it.”"
"5218","I do not like to start giving a sermon, but the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to recite this supplication after finishing the meal: ""All praise is exclusively for Allah, such praise that is abundant, pure, blessed, not forsaken, and not dispensed with."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) This narration has been heard by Mu'awiyah bin Salih from 'Amir bin Jashib, and by Buheir bin Sa'd from Khalid bin Ma'dan, so both its chains are preserved."
"5219","I also went along with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had eaten the food and washed his hands, he recited this: ""All praise is due to Allah alone, Who feeds and is not fed, Who has bestowed favor upon us and guided us, Who has given us food to eat, given us drink, and placed us in a good condition. All praise is due to Allah alone, Who has fed from the food, given drink from the drink, clothed the unclothed body, and guided from misguidance, Who granted sight to the blind, and has given us superiority over many of His creation. All praise is due to Allah alone, the Lord of all the worlds."
"5220","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ate or drank, he said: ""Praise be to Allah Who has given food and drink and made it easy to swallow, and provided an exit for it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3851)"
"5221","Ibn ‘Abbas said that his maternal aunt presented to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ clarified butter, lizards and cottage cheese. He ate from clarified butter and cheese, but left the lizard abominably. It was eaten on the food cloth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Had it been unlawful, it would not have been eaten on the food cloth of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3793)"
"5222","I have eaten it at the table of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"5223","The sister of my mother Umm Hufaid presented to Messenger of Allah ﷺ clarified butter (ghee), cheese and some lizards. He ate out of the clarified butter and cheese, but left the lizard finding no liking for it. But it was eaten on the table of Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Had it been forbidden (haram), it could not be eaten on the table of Messenger of Allah ﷺ. (Using translation from Muslim 1947)"
"5224","The people said, ""O Messenger of Allah! We eat but do not feel satiated."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""Do you eat together or separately?"" They replied, ""We eat separately."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Eat together and mention the name of Allah over it. There will be blessing in it for you."
"5225","Jabir reported that Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a man should eat with the left hand or walk with one sandal or wrap himself completely leaving no opening for the arms (to draw out) or support himself when sitting with a single garment wrapped round his knees which may expose his private parts. (Using translation from Muslim 2099a)"
"5226","When any one of you intends to eat (meal), he should eat with his right hand. and when he (intends) to drink he should drink with his right hand, for the Satan eats with his left hand and drinks with his left hand. (Using translation from Muslim 2020a)"
"5227","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to reserve his right hand for eating and his left hand for other tasks. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator named Abu Ayyub is Abdullah bin Ali Afriki."
"5228","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) forbade a person from giving or taking anything with the left hand, and he also forbade breathing into the vessel while drinking water."
"5229","narrates from his father that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""No person should eat with his left hand nor drink with it, because Satan eats with it and drinks with it."" Nafi' has narrated these additional words in his narration: ""Do not take with it and do not give with it."
"5230","The example of a believer is like that of a date palm tree; if he eats, he eats what is pure, and if he stores, he stores what is pure."
"5231","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) passed by us and said: Do not eat (two dates) together, because the Noble Pr"
"5232","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Whoever is eating dates with people should not eat two dates together; if he intends to do so, he should seek their permission. If they permit him, then he may do so.\"""""
"5233","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) sent us Ajwah dates, and they were poured out among us. Due to the severity of hunger, we began to eat two dates at a time. Whenever any one of us ate two dates together, he would say to his companion, ""I am eating two together, so you also eat two together."
"5234","“The believer eats with one intestine and the disbeliever eats with seven intestines.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3256)"
"5235","A believer drinks In one intestine whereas a non-believer drinks in seven intestines. (Using translation from Muslim 2063)"
"5236","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: “No vessel that a human fills is worse than his stomach. O son of Adam, it is sufficient for you to eat a few morsels that keep your back straight. But if you must (eat more), then (fill) one third (of your stomach) with food, one third with water, and one third with air (for breathing).”"
"5237","“The food of one person is sufficient for two, the food of two is sufficient for four, and the food for four is sufficient for eight.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3254)"
"5238","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: \""A Muslim eats with one intestine, and a disbeliever eats with seven intestines.\"""""
"5239","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""A believer eats in one intestine, and a disbeliever eats in seven intestines.\"" The Shaykh says: This narration is exactly in accordance with the condition of human beings."""
"5240","I do not eat while reclining. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3769)"
"5241","The Prophet ﷺ was brought a piece of cheese in Tabuk. He called for a knife, mentioned Allah's name and cut it. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3819)"
"5242","I do not eat that meat which you people (i.e., the people of Makkah) slaughter in the name of idols. We only eat that upon which Allah's name has been mentioned."
